{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/896128-your-terrible-wings","id":896128,"title":"Your Terrible Wings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-22T10:03:11-07:00","id":896128,"title":"Your Terrible Wings","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Blood and Smoke, page 70</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Humanity is a half-forgotten dream. Elders are the unmarked grave of many. The names on the tombstones dotting your shriveled soul are worn nearly smooth. You are no longer just a vampire, you\u2019ve evolved into something alien and inscrutable. You are the pupa for something even more unknowable. All you need to do is survive the long chrysalis, and you might get to spread your terrible wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a wonderful quote and, with <i>A Thousand Years of Night</i> still a long way away, I started having fun brainstorming the idea of elder vampires evolving into something <i>other</i>. I threw together a few concepts, two for each Clan linked to Clan themes and Disciplines, for people to enjoy (some better than others \u2013 Daeva was tricky) but I\u2019m interested in hearing people\u2019s ideas (the crazier the better) and what other people have done in their games.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Perfect Face<br /> This Serpent hides its face, wearing masks, hoods and scarves. It does this because to look upon its androgynous face is to fall in love. Or perhaps, more accurately, fall into supplication. Mortals who gaze upon the perfect visage weep and beg to serve, if only to be in the presence of this god among mortals. Kindred are more resistant but even they are not immune. This Serpent rules a huge cult and could quite feasibly star tan entire religion, if it were not for the Masquerade. If it was brave enough it could cast aside its masks and become a literal God in the eyes of many.<br /> <br /> Vital Body<br /> As vampires age they generally become paler, less human. This elder Daeva, over the last few centuries, noticed that the opposite seemed to be happening. Her skin has grown warm to the touch, without the pallor of death. She exudes vitality and life and, of late, has found her Beast\u2019s voice quieter, her fear of fire entirely absent. She has even begun waking from the daysleep at dawn, without the enervation Kindred experience while the sun reigns. One question remains, a terrifying question; can she face the sun?<br /> <br /> King of Beasts<br /> All animals are cowed by this alpha predator. They submit, instantly, and obey it utterly. The most devoted pet would turn on its master if this Gangrel wished. Birds whisper secrets to it, spy for it. Other Kindred are terrified of this vampire, not least because their own Beasts respond to it. They are compelled to serve this creature and terrified of the consequences of disloyalty. Most terrifying of all, Draugr and revenants obey it with and have been used to tear apart those who have displeased this Savage.<br /> <br /> Truly Protean<br /> This vampire\u2019s ability to change its form had grown far beyond that of others. It is able to twist its visage into that of other Kindred or humans, to copy animals without having tasted their blood, even splitting its consciousness across multiple bodies for short periods. It also takes joy in creating new, impossible forms and using its shapeshifting abilities to hunt prey. It enjoys challenges and variety in its hunts. Sometimes it will take only human forms, stalking its prey in disguise. Other time it will take wing, or harry prey as a pack of dogs (or dog-like <i>things)</i>, while on occasion it may take a truly monstrous or outright impossible shape.<br /> <br /> All-Seeing Eye<br /> This elder Shadow is barely seen by the Kindred of its city. Few even know that it exists, and to most that do it\u2019s just known as a reclusive elder uninvolved in the politics of the city. This is far from true, however. This Mekhet sees all in its astral form, sees through the eyes of kine and kindred and beast, knows everything that happens in its domain. It acts behind the scenes, influencing events, from time to time but this vampire is far more content to watch than to act. Its body, which it barely inhabits, is an anchor increasingly irrelevant to this vampire, an anchor and a weakness it hopes to transcend. <br /> <br /> Living Shadow<br /> Form, solidity... these are increasingly optional to this Mehket. It is difficult to make out facial features or even the gender of this vampire, who is forever shrouded in darkness, save for its glimmering eyes. It can disappear from sight and reappear from other patches of darkness in the blink of an eye, faster even than would be expected from a master of Celerity. Its indistinct shape also seems malleable, and of late its arms have begun appearing as wings.<br /> <br /> Fear Itself<br /> All Nosferatu are unsettling to be near. Their territories gradually darken and become more frightening. This elder\u2019s aura of fear, of <i>wrongness</i> has spread over an entire city and beyond. Recurrent nightmares are increasingly a fact of life within it's ever-widening sphere of influence and a vague impression of its shape has become a local legend and an internet meme. Stylized graffiti of its claws has begun appearing on wall and in underpasses, even though few have ever seen them. For its part, the vampire struggles <i>not</i> to terrify and terrorise. Other Kindred can hardly stand to be in its presence and it has become <i>de facto </i>ruler of the nightmare city.<br /> <br /> The Gentleman<br /> Humanity and identity have become distant memories to this vampire. It seldom appears, preferring to live behind a veil of Obfuscate, but even when it does people struggle to remember anything of its appearance, recalling only a blank face and that it was terrifying to be near but even more terrifying to flee and risk its displeasure. This vampire has grown so inhuman that is spends much of its time watching people, occasionally making strange request or abducting them in a vain attempt to understand what it meant to be human and to have a face and a name.<br /> <br /> Fisher King<br /> This Ventrue has been Prince for centuries and now it seems almost unthinkable to depose him, for on some level he has become one with his kingdom. It is responsive to his moods \u2013 dangerous when he is angry, stable when he is calm. Spikes in crime, accidents and wild animal attacks occur during his rages and once, when he was almost killed, earthquakes ravaged the city. The Kindred must appease their Prince and even his most hated rivals fear the consequences of killing him.<br /> <br /> In The Blood<br /> A Lord is used to commanding others and even wearing their flesh when it suits her purposes. Over time, her influence over those she had bitten grew stronger and stranger. They began to preempt her whims and she began to experience snippets of sensory inputs from her ghouls and blood dolls. She\u2019s realised, now, what\u2019s happening \u2013 her consciousness is splitting, spreading across the bodies touched by her blood and her Curse. She is the Curse itself made sentient.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 05-22-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":29}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:39:52-07:00","id":896151,"title":"","content":"That is fun, inspiring stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d