strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/896128-your-terrible-wings?p=897203#post897203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This dovetails so well with Beast... I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fully intentional. Likewise how the Living Shadow's wings and shadow-powers are very reminiscent of the Strix...<br /> <br /> Thanks for the kind words, but let's keep this ball rolling!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:57:16-07:00","id":897393,"title":"","content":"I would love to see Devotions that are permanently &quot;on&quot; - kind of like Coils of the Dragon that aren't <i>entirely</i> passive.<br /> <br /> Things that... like it... when your Humanity is low, and your Blood Potency is high.<br /> <br /> Auspex Devotions that let you smell the sweet, sweet sin on the breath of those around you.<br /> <br /> Majesty Devotions that worm you into memories - you met them today, but they could have sworn that had been you, so many years ago, who gave them their first kiss...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:50:00-07:00","id":897534,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>: It sounds like Falco1029's <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OyVs-12emmgTK6XSu6dgmACqv7B8TpZuJv2z-9A7yxw/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Elder Transmutations</b></a> might be right up your alley.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar452_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"452\" data-vbnamecard=\"452\">Eremite</a>: \u200bI especially like &quot;Fear Itself&quot;. I assume that its status as both urban legend and internet meme is a nod to the Slender Man. You inspired me to try and write one. Any feedback is very welcome.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For those ancient Ventrue who have maintained an iron grip over their domains for centuries, the notion that they are big fishes in small ponds is laughable. They do not comprehend the patience and cunning of the truly dead. These monolithic guardians of the other side have no children or sire, no strings to pull or hearts to bewitch. But for all the reach of their frigid eyes, there are tales of Kindred who fell into their lands and managed to escape.<br /> <br /> One of them is supposedly a cloaked figure with filthy bandages over their eyes, and no tongue or lower jaw. On its back are broken stubs of wings, and a Strix is perched on its arm like a trained falcon. This entity has been named the Vulture due to its habit of invading domains that have been torn apart by the Strix and only have a few survivors. These Kindred who think themselves safe or innocent are patiently stalked by the Vulture, who sends its Strix to torment and weaken the survivors until they can't fight back anymore. In other times, he stalks those who are loved by many in a peaceful city. The Vulture takes them to a subterranean place filled with perfect darkness, and they are never seen again.<br /> <br /> They say that the Vulture was a Ventrue who struck a bargain with a god of the dead. He is searching for a number of Kindred to fill a prison, or one who has committed specific and unforgivable crimes. He was disfigured as a symbolic punishment and a reminder of the wrongs he must right. Only when he completes this mission will he be set free. None of this can be confirmed with supernatural or mundane investigation directed at the Vulture himself. The Strix who accompanies him says that the kidnapped are sent to their homes, and that those who want to visit them one last time are free to follow. So far, all those who accepted have suffered the final death, and their remains were found smeared over the entrance to the earth below.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: Dammit, I just realized this is really similar to a Huntsman. I don't know how to fix this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-24-2016, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T02:18:06-07:00","id":897646,"title":"","content":"I feel like The Unholy is an elder soaring on her terrible wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chec